Subject: [PATCH] firmware_class: look in /system/etc/firmware

The kernel looks for firmware files under /lib/firmware, which Android does not have;
they are in /system/etc/firmware. So every file is asked of ueventd, with a uevent,
and that matters at each suspend: on the way down the kernel caches again all the
firmware it has handed out (the WiFi's, the video core's, the touch controller's).
A process that waits for uevents with EPOLLWAKEUP (the health HAL does) holds a
wakeup source from the moment one arrives until it has read it. Freezing user space then
aborts, after about 5 ms, and suspend is tried again a minute later, with the same
result: on LineageOS 20 the tablet never suspended, through a whole night.

Read straight from /system/etc/firmware, the files need no uevent. ueventd stays the
way for anything asked before /system is mounted.
---
--- drivers/base/firmware_class.c
+++ drivers/base/firmware_class.c
@@ -298,7 +298,9 @@
 	"/lib/firmware/updates",
 	"/lib/firmware/" UTS_RELEASE,
 	"/lib/firmware",
-	"/firmware/image"
+	"/firmware/image",
+	/* Android's, where the files are; /lib is not there at all. */
+	"/system/etc/firmware"
 };
 
 /*
